---
/**
 * Problem.astro — One tight beat on the problem: pasted-prompt chaos.
 */
---

<section class="section problem" id="problem" aria-labelledby="problem-title" data-reveal-section>
  <div class="section-shell">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="kicker eyebrow scroll-in">The problem</p>
      <h2 id="problem-title" class="scroll-in" style="--delay:80ms">Pasted prompts. No record. No governance.</h2>
      <p class="section-lede scroll-in" style="--delay:160ms">
        Right now, coordinating agents means pasting the same prompt into every window
        and hoping nothing drifts. No shared state, no ordered delivery, no evidence gate —
        just copy-paste and crossed fingers.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="bezel scroll-in" style="--delay:240ms" role="img" aria-label="A pasted-prompt chaos card showing uncoordinated agent instructions">
      <div class="bezel__core problem-card">
        <div class="problem-card__header">
          <span class="problem-card__dot problem-card__dot--red"></span>
          <span class="problem-card__dot problem-card__dot--amber"></span>
          <span class="problem-card__dot problem-card__dot--green"></span>
          <span class="problem-card__title">agent-instructions.md — pasted 5×</span>
        </div>
        <div class="problem-card__body">
          <pre class="problem-card__code"><code>You are agent-a. Read handoff.txt and continue the work.
Make sure you don't duplicate what agent-b did.
The scope is: the retry boundary in handoff.txt.
Report back when done. Do not claim tasks that aren't yours.</code></pre>
          <div class="problem-card__chaos">
            <span class="problem-card__tag problem-card__tag--conflict">agent-a sees v1</span>
            <span class="problem-card__tag problem-card__tag--conflict">agent-b sees v3</span>
            <span class="problem-card__tag problem-card__tag--conflict">agent-c sees v2</span>
            <span class="problem-card__tag problem-card__tag--stale">agent-d: stale scope</span>
            <span class="problem-card__tag problem-card__tag--stale">agent-e: no fencing</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="problem-foot scroll-in" style="--delay:320ms">
      MCP is the tool protocol your hosts already speak. Weft adds the
      coordination layer on top — rooms, consent, addressing, and an evidence gate.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
